== Harness notes (cost me two false starts) ==
- `&` inside a Bash tool call gets reaped: the driver died instantly and
  reported exit 0. Use the harness's own run_in_background instead.
- A pinned binary needs libfreeciv.so BESIDE it: RUNPATH is `$ORIGIN/`,
  so a bare `cp build/freeciv-server` pin fails every game with
  "cannot open shared object file". Pins are directories now.

== Items 6 and 7: PARKED, with the evidence the brief asked for ==

Item 6 (the Defend_Bonus sweep, audit 2c). The defect is confirmed and
its seam is named, but the work is not done.

  civ2civ3 has 13 Defend_Bonus effects across FOUR distinct carriers
  that answer distinct threat classes -- City Walls (Ground), Coastal
  Defense (sea), SAM Battery (air), SDI Defense -- plus Great Library
  / Research Lab / Cathedral entries that are not defence carriers at
  all.

  Both deep and stock reduce that whole family to ONE building:
  dai_find_source_building(pcity, EFT_DEFEND_BONUS, NULL), under
  stock's own comment "HACK: This needs changing if multiple
  improvements provide this effect" (daimilitary.c:1896, and again at
  :962). Deep inherited the hack at deepdefence.c:4210, where
  wall_fear_weight routes ALL injected fear -- boat shadow, air,
  barbarian, density -- into whichever single building that call
  happens to return. So the coastal fear a city carries can be paying
  for City Walls, which do nothing about ships.

  Not built here because the brief says park rather than rush, and
