== 16:45 The item-5 census, and why it forced a seventh commit ==

The A/B I started at 16:11 was measuring nothing, and the counter is
what said so: ZERO deep-upcharge lines in the ON arm.

Instrumented one 40-turn contested game, logging every candidate that
reached the charge and the upkeep it read:

    616 evaluations reached deep_unit_upkeep_charge()
    321 of them got as far as reading an upkeep
      5 were actually charged

    pick / upkeep as read                            n
    Settlers   ups=0 upg=0 upf=1  Despotism         184
    Settlers   ups=0 upg=0 upf=1  Tribal             75
    Settlers   ups=0 upg=0 upf=1  Anarchy            22
    Diplomat   ups=0 upg=0 upf=0  Despotism          14
    Phalanx    ups=0 upg=0 upf=1  Despotism           7
    Workers    ups=0 upg=0 upf=0  Despotism           8
    Warriors   ups=0 upg=0 upf=1  Despotism           4
    Phalanx    ups=1 upg=0 upf=1  Tribal              2
    ... (the rest are ones and twos)

**Under Despotism, Tribal and Anarchy -- the governments deep is in
for most of a contested game -- civ2civ3 charges almost every unit NO
gold and NO shields. The only nonzero upkeep in the venue is FOOD.**

So excluding food did not under-charge in the "safe direction" the
commit message claimed; it charged nothing at all. Worse, the audit's
own headline population is a SETTLER, and a settler's whole lifetime
cost in this ruleset IS the food that suppresses the city it came
from.

Fixed in 9275e9bb6d by summing gold + food under upkeep_gold_weight,
which is the equivalence deep_defender_upkeep_discount() (same file,
forty lines up) already makes. After: 299 charges a game, 281 of them
Settlers.

SECOND FINDING, and it is the more interesting one. The charge is now
correctly dimensioned and still tiny against what it is subtracted
from:

    deep-upcharge ... pick="Settlers" life=24 upf=1 debit=3.0
                      want=750.1 left=747.1

3 want against 750 is 0.4%. upkeep_gold_weight is 0.125, so even at
the top of unit_upkeep_charge's registered range (4.0) the charge is
1.6% of a settler bid. **The mechanism cannot move this auction, and
the reason is not the mechanism.** A charge calibrated on the BUILDING
side (where a 1-gold building costs 3 want against credits of tens) is
invisible on the UNIT side, where a scaled domestic settler bid is
750. That is RC4 -- incommensurable want scales -- measured, with a
ratio attached. It is W01's problem, not this seat's, and I am not
widening the knob range to paper over it because picking that width
would be inventing a constant.

Expect the item-5-alone A/B to be null. It is being run anyway,
because the brief asked for it and because a null with a census
attached is a result.

